    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n79986" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾰτᾰγ-έω</span></b> , 
			Aeol.
		
		impf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πατάγεσκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alc.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					25.9
				</span></i>
			 :— <i>clatter, clash</i>, of the sharp loud noise
			caused by the collision of two bodies, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				378s
			</span></i>q. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαρὺ δ᾽ ἄγριοι χειμῶνες παταγεῦσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anacr.
					6
				</span></i>
			 ; of Bacchants, Pratin.Lyr.<i><span class="en">
				1.3
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὼ δὲ πίθω πατάγεσκ᾽ ὀ
			πύθμην</span> Alc.l.c. ; of the sea, <i>dash, plash</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				22.15
			</span></i> ; <i>chatter</i>, as birds, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				168
			</span></i> (anap.) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ κόττυφος ἐν μὲν τῷ θέρει ᾄδει,
					τοῦ δὲ χειμῶνος παταγεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					632b17
				</span></i>
			 ; <i>gnash</i>, as teeth, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Im.</u>
				1.28
			</span></i> : prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλὰ δὴ παταγεῖς</span>
			<i>well hit!</i> prob. from the game described under <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλαταγών</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				116
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> trans.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύμπανα π</span>. <i>beat</i> drums,
				<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Syr.D.</u>
				50
			</span></i> :—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἷς ἔντεα παταγεῖται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Lyr.Adesp.</u>
					121
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαταγεῖτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Tim.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			.</div>
